      <h1>The Cross Timbers</h1>
      <p>
        A band of post oak and blackjack oak timber running through
        north-central Texas, where eastern woods meet western prairie. It's
        the home ground of Honest Acres Group — our owner's ranch is in
        Comanche County, in the heart of it.
      </p>

      <h2>The land</h2>
      <p>
        Sandy loam soils under native and improved pasture, oak motts and
        creek bottoms, and farm ponds in nearly every pasture. It's some of
        the most versatile ground in Texas: the same tract can run cattle,
        cut Bermuda hay, and hunt well in the fall.
      </p>

      <h2>Why buyers come here</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Production:</strong> real grazing and hay country, not just scenery.<br />
        <strong>Wildlife:</strong> whitetail, turkey, dove, and hogs in the oak-and-pasture mix.<br />
        <strong>Water:</strong> tanks, creeks, and practical well country.<br />
        <strong>Value:</strong> priced on what the land does — historically below the famous-name regions, for ground that often out-produces them.
      </p>

      <h2>Counties we know best here</h2>
      <p>Comanche, Erath, Eastland, Brown, Hamilton, Mills, and Coleman — see the <a href="/county-guides/">county guides</a> for detail by county.</p>

